[
  {
    "_comment": "CAPABILITY suite for BigQuery bulk dest (full matrix incl. schema evolution `update`), via `--type connectors/bigquery.json`. Functions in functions/caps_bigquery.py; input from dev datagen caps_input. Targets are backtick-quoted (resolve project.dataset.table from the conn). append/replace on cap_append/cap_replace. SCHEMA EVOLUTION two-phase: run caps_evo_v1 -> bigquery_evolve_v1 creates cap_evolve (narrow); THEN trigger caps_evo_v2 -> bigquery_evolve_v2 appends wide with schema_evolution=update (ALLOW_FIELD_ADDITION). caps_evo_v2 not auto-triggered. Domains: dev, bigquery. MERGE (if_table_exists=\"merge\", CDC markers i/u/d/l/t): the 12 batches of functions/_merge_plan.py, each a caps_input publisher caps_merge_<batch> (functions/caps_merge_batches.py) and a bigquery_out subscriber bigquery_merge_<batch> onto the batch's target keyed on cap_id, marker in op (bigquery.schema_evolution_engine=iceberg, which a merge requires). Not auto-triggered: after the monitor, an actions stage triggers them in order (a non-detached tdk fn trigger, which waits for the merge) and after each reads the target from BigQuery itself (scripts/verify_merge.py, tagged check) and fails unless it holds exactly the rows the plan says. cap_merge: b1 creates it, b2 is an initial load over stale rows, b3 coalesces several changes per key, b4 truncates, b5 merges onto the empty table, b6 loads then truncates mid-batch (the last reset wins), b7 merges onto what it left, b8 is an initial load of an empty table (a bare l). cap_merge_from_load: load1 is an initial load as the first write, load2 merges onto what it created. cap_merge_from_truncate: trunc1 is a bare t as the first write (an empty table), trunc2 merges onto it. A load is only ever a batch's first row, as a CDC source emits it."
  },
  {
    "domain-manifest": {
      "domains": [
        {
          "name": "${xp:name(dev)}",
          "system": "dev"
        },
        {
          "name": "${xp:name(bigquery)}",
          "system": "bigquery"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "collections": [
      {
        "name": "caps_input",
        "type": "datagen_in",
        "connection_template": "connection-file:connections/datagen_in.yaml",
        "group": "sources",
        "domains": {
          "D0": "${xp:name(dev)}"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "bigquery_out",
        "type": "bigquery_bulk_out",
        "connection_template": "connection-file:connections/bigquery_bulk_out.yaml",
        "group": "destinations",
        "domains": {
          "D0": "${xp:name(bigquery)}"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
